    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0406" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Maginnis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-28T17:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 29—10:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your 3, January 27, 5 p.m. Saavedra inaugurated this afternoon, will probably
                    announce Cabinet within next few days. Convention will now take up various
                    proposed amendments to Constitution including question, whether or not it will
                    constitute itself the Congress of Bolivia or call for elections.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d237-f1"/> Railway strike settled today. Situation perfectly
                    tranquil. Understand minority will return to convention tomorrow or Monday. In
                    my opinion there is no danger of disturbances at present, only question is
                    whether Saavedra will secure cooperation of other leaders in forming strong
                    government. I suggest waiting for few days before recognizing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Maginnis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d237-f1" n="2" xml:id="d237-f1-content">
                <p>The convention voted June 17, 1921, to constitute itself the Congress of Bolivia
                    (file no. 824.00/217).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
